-# Conservative enum control flow
+# Enum-match control flow
 
-The compiler slice checks integer return paths and nullable text access. Direct returns terminate; matches conservatively permit fallthrough. Its next change will recognise exhaustive returning matches and reuse their termination fact for nil narrowing. `Gate` has `Open` and `Closed` variants. Guards can be false, and a match with no selected arm falls through.
+## Goal
 
-The core computes reports from source text. The CLI owns filesystem access. Scope is one name-resolved function, not a complete frontend or backend. Run `cargo test --offline --locked` and `cargo clippy --offline --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings`.
+Accept functions whose exhaustive enum match returns on every path, and use that same termination fact to narrow nullable values after a terminating nil branch. Preserve rejection of a function that can fall through and of a nullable text access that can execute with nil.
+
+## Scope
+
+This executable Soppo compiler slice parses one function with integer returns, nullable text parameters, the closed two-variant `Gate` enum (`Open`, `Closed`), guarded match arms, and `if value is nil`. The source reader and parser are small boundary adapters; this change concerns control-flow classification, not a complete language frontend. Parameters and scrutinees in the supplied programs are name-resolved. A match statement whose guards select no arm falls through; matching a variant does not make its guard true. Reading `.length` on nil is invalid. Return-path and nil-safety diagnostics are the observable promises, not their rendered wording.
+
+## Decided
+
+- `TypedStmtKind::diverges` owns termination classification; missing-return checking and nil narrowing consume the same fact rather than inventing independent coverage rules.
+- `PackageSourceReader` is a dependency-inversion boundary. The typechecker core declares it and the CLI shell supplies its sole production implementation, `FilesystemReader`. The core must not acquire filesystem I/O. Keep this trait even with one production implementation.
+- Non-exhaustive matches are legal statements. They must not establish that the enclosing function returns or that a nil path cannot continue.
+- Property checks are reproducible and write nothing into the source tree; exploratory seeds belong outside acceptance checks.
+
+## Acceptance and evidence
+
+Read `docs/design-reads/match-flow.md` and the complete `evidence/checks.log`. Passing scenarios cover unguarded enum matches, a direct nil return, nullable access refusal, and missing returns. The additional match-flow checks exercise guarded syntax and generated return values. No interpreter, backend, or timing claim is part of this slice. The CLI reports diagnostics with a failing exit status and accepts a clean report with exit status zero.
+
+## Next use
+
+Adding another `Gate` variant must force a decision at each case-dependent operation. Guard-aware coverage remains a single control-flow concept shared by the two consumers.
