 # Match-flow design read
 
-`TypedStmtKind::diverges` recognises direct returns. Both missing-return checking and nil narrowing consume that fact. Match statements conservatively fall through, even when every variant has a returning arm. This refuses some valid programs but never infers termination merely from a guarded arm's presence.
+## Models and consumers
 
-The planned change adds enum coverage to that shared predicate. `MatchArm::guard` is retained in the AST, and a false guard allows continuation when no later arm matches. `GateVariant` is a closed set with `Open` and `Closed`. The CLI owns source-file reads; the core computes over values.
+`src/ast.rs` owns `TypedStmtKind::diverges` and the closed `GateVariant` set. `src/infer.rs` uses block termination for missing-return checking and for removing a nullable binding after its nil branch cannot continue. `src/parser.rs` preserves guards as arm data. `src/main.rs` implements the source-reader boundary and owns filesystem I/O.
+
+## Disagreements
+
+| Concept | Representations | Current relationship |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Enum coverage | `GateVariant::ALL`, arm patterns | Coverage counts appearances of every variant; bodies must all terminate. |
+| Guard selection | `MatchArm::guard`, runtime parameter | A false guard skips its arm; an uncovered runtime path continues after the match. |
+| Termination | AST method, inference consumers | Both missing-return checking and nil narrowing trust the AST fact. |
+
+## Source sample
+
+Read `TypedStmtKind::diverges`, `check_block`, `check_function`, `tests/scenarios.rs`, and `tests/match_flow.rs`. The parser keeps both guarded and unguarded forms. The source reader is not another control-flow model: it supplies bytes to the core without giving the core an I/O dependency.
+
+## Decisions and limits
+
+The single termination predicate avoids independent approximations in the two consumers. A complete enum spelling is not alone proof that an arm executes; the language permits guarded matches to fall through. The next variant addition should require explicit decisions, rather than inheriting a wildcard's behaviour.
